1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:02,320
This is an AI customer support agent.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:09,280
A customer emails a question about their order, the agent reads the thread and then looks up the answer in the knowledge base and creates a reply.

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:13,680
Anything it isn't sure about, it escalates to a human agent in this dashboard.

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:17,920
In this course, you will learn AI engineering by building this system from scratch.

5
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:22,788
And the example comes from real client work at my AI development company, Datalumina.

6
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:27,760
We have helped six companies automate their entire customer support using this exact system.

7
00:00:27,918 --> 00:00:30,800
And we are going to build all of this, so no shortcuts.

8
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:47,120
The Gmail connection, the API with Fast API, the agent and its tools with Pydentic AI and Claude, a superbased database, e-files to test the agent, a React admin dashboard, and last but not least, a real deployment to a server via Docker using Hostinger.

9
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:53,840
And most tutorials and courses that you'll find here on YouTube only really cover the LLM API calls, but not in this one.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
We really go full stack end-to-end.

