00:45:41,600 --> 00:45:44,560
So it pulls data on a certain rhythm.

638
00:45:44,846 --> 00:45:50,080
Now, this is different from working with what's known as webhooks.

639
00:45:50,240 --> 00:45:53,760
So you can see polling or webhooks, there's a little bit of an explanation in here.

640
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:56,320
And polling is generally easier.

641
00:45:56,654 --> 00:46:00,560
Working with webhooks is generally a more production best practice.

642
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:02,560
So a webhook is instant.

643
00:46:02,766 --> 00:46:12,320
So a webhook would mean every time a new email lands in our inbox, the Gmail server would directly send a message to our backend.

644
00:46:12,560 --> 00:46:13,668
So we have that connection.

645
00:46:13,870 --> 00:46:14,960
So it's like instant.

646
00:46:15,040 --> 00:46:16,036
We know it exactly.

647
00:46:16,398 --> 00:46:26,400
Polling is pretty much stating every five minutes from our server, we initiate a call towards Gmail and check did something happen in the last five minutes?

648
00:46:26,480 --> 00:46:28,000
And if yes, we pull the data.

649
00:46:28,238 --> 00:46:29,680
So there are two different approaches.

650
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:34,628
And why I wanted to go with polling in this setup is because it's way easier to set up.

651
00:46:34,880 --> 00:46:38,720
